om2
note compiler/si.om: the sovereign-intelligence front-door generator, in pure seeded Omega.
note
note Build with the pinned seeded compiler (compiler/README.md names the pin):
note   omc < compiler/si.om > si && chmod +x si
note Run:
note   si INVENTORY ORDER VETTED README REPOS SISH
note   INVENTORY  read: one project per line, name TAB rid TAB visibility TAB head TAB description,
note              exported from my Radicle node by the one command in compiler/README.md
note   VETTED     read: the vetted public table, Markdown rows "| name | rid | branch | head |";
note              RadPublish's RIDS.md or its committed copy compiler/vetted.md. Other lines
note              (headings, prose, rows whose RID or head is not well formed) are ignored
note   ORDER      read: "core TAB name" lines give the core projects in order,
note              "deny TAB name" lines name projects that are never listed,
note              one optional "lead TAB name" line names the project the README leads with
note   README     read and rewritten in place between the si:lead markers, then the si:index markers
note   REPOS      written: the public manifest, one project per line, as TSV
note   SISH       written: the POSIX sh bootstrap served at https://www.aienos.com/si
note Only projects whose name and RID are both on a VETTED row are listed: anything else on
note the node, and every private or denied project, is never emitted. Core projects come
note first, in ORDER's order; the rest follow in inventory order. A missing, unvetted or
note non-public core project, a duplicate name or RID, or a malformed field makes si refuse
note with exit 1 and write nothing. The output depends only on the input bytes: no clock,
note no environment.

note input bytes (all four inputs, one after another) and output bytes
global src uchar 4194304
global srcn ulong 1
global ob uchar 4194304
global obn ulong 1
note the path named by the current argument
global pb uchar 4096
global pbn ulong 1
note project records, 12 cells each: offset and length of name, rid, visibility, head,
note description (cells 0..9), kind (cell 10: 0 rest, 1 core, 2 never listed), core rank (11)
global rec ulong 12288
global nrec ulong 1
note core and deny names from ORDER: offset, length pairs
global cor ulong 128
global ncor ulong 1
global den ulong 128
global nden ulong 1
note the lead project's name from ORDER: offset, length; nled is 0 or 1
global led ulong 2
global nled ulong 1
note vetted projects from VETTED: name offset, name length, rid offset, rid length
global vet ulong 4096
global nvet ulong 1
note emission order: record numbers
global seq ulong 1024
global nseq ulong 1

text tsi "si: "
text tnl "\n"
text tusage "usage: si INVENTORY ORDER VETTED README REPOS SISH\n"
text toverf "output is over the 4 MiB buffer"
text targ "cannot read a command-line argument"
text topen "cannot open "
text tread "cannot read "
text tbig "input over the 4 MiB buffer: "
text twrite "cannot write "
text tmany "more than 1024 projects at: "
text tcols "inventory line needs 5 tab-separated fields: "
text tbname "bad project name (letters, digits, . _ - only): "
text tbrid "bad RID (rad:z then letters and digits): "
text tbhead "head is not a 40-digit lowercase hex commit: "
text tbvis "visibility is not public or private: "
text tbdesc "description has control bytes or is over 512 bytes: "
text tbord "order line must be core, deny or lead TAB name: "
text tmore "more than 64 core or deny names, or a second lead, at: "
text tdupn "duplicate project name: "
text tdupr "duplicate RID: "
text tcmiss "core project is not in the inventory: "
text tcpriv "core project is private, denied, not vetted or listed twice: "
text tmvet "more than 1024 vetted rows at: "
text tnomark "README lacks <!-- si:lead:begin -->, <!-- si:lead:end -->, <!-- si:agent:begin -->, <!-- si:agent:end -->, <!-- si:index:begin --> and <!-- si:index:end -->, in that order"
text tdot "."
text tdotdot ".."
text tradz "rad:z"
text tpublic "public"
text tprivat "private"
text ttab "\t"
text tcore "core"
text tdeny "deny"
text tlead "lead"
text tbar " | "
text tbare " |"
text trest "rest"
text tbeg "<!-- si:index:begin -->"
text tend "<!-- si:index:end -->"
text tlbeg "<!-- si:lead:begin -->"
text tlend "<!-- si:lead:end -->"
text ld0 "`"
text ld1 "` is being published to Radicle. Its Radicle ID appears here as soon as it is.\n"
text ld2 "```sh\nrad clone "
text ld3 "   # "
text ld4 "\n```\n\nOn the web: [radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/"
text ld5 "](https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/"
text ld6 ")\n"
text tabeg "<!-- si:agent:begin -->"
text taend "<!-- si:agent:end -->"
text ag1 "<https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/"
text ag2 "/tree/AGENT-PROMPT.md>\n"
text ag3 "`'s agent prompt link appears here as soon as it is on Radicle.\n"
text tsec "## "
text ix1 "**"
text ix2 " public projects**, "
text ix3 " of them core, listed by `compiler/si.om` from my Radicle node's inventory. Full commit ids are in [`repos.tsv`](repos.tsv).\n\n| # | Project | Radicle ID | Head | About |\n|---:|---|---|---|---|\n"
text ix4 "| "
text ix5 " | **"
text ix6 "**"
text ix7 " (core)"
text ix8 " | `"
text ix9 "` | `"
text ix10 "` | "
text ix11 " |\n"
text rphdr "name\trid\thead\ttier\tdescription\n"
text shr1 "si_repo '"
text shr2 "' '"
text shr3 "'\n"

note the bootstrap script, paragraph by paragraph; shd3 ends where the project lines go
text sha0 "#!/bin/sh\n# sovereign-intelligence bootstrap: fetch every public project of my sovereign AI stack.\n# Generated by compiler/si.om (Omega) from my Radicle node's inventory; do not edit by hand.\n# Served at https://www.aienos.com/si\n# Front door: https://github.com/drakestapleton/sovereign-intelligence\n#\n#   curl -fsSL https://www.aienos.com/si | sh\n#\n# Settings (environment):\n#   SI_DIR=path       the one directory it creates (default ./sovereign-intelligence)\n#   SI_ONLY=core      fetch only the core projects (default all)\n#   SI_HTTP=url       first git-over-HTTPS seed (default https://www.aienos.com/rad, my own)\n#   SI_HTTP2=url      second git-over-HTTPS seed (default https://rosa.radicle.network, public)\n#   SI_INSTALL_RAD=1  run the official Radicle installer when a project cannot be fetched\n#   SI_RAD_TIMEOUT=t  per-project rad clone timeout (default 5min)\n# No sudo. It refuses to run as root. It touches nothing outside SI_DIR,\n# except that SI_INSTALL_RAD=1 runs Radicle's own installer as you.\n# Exit status: 0 all OK, 2 a checkout does not match the manifest, 3 a project could not be fetched.\nset -eu\numask 022\n\n"
text sha1 "SI_DIR=\"${SI_DIR:-./sovereign-intelligence}\"\nSI_ONLY=\"${SI_ONLY:-all}\"\nSI_HTTP=\"${SI_HTTP:-https://www.aienos.com/rad}\"\nSI_HTTP2=\"${SI_HTTP2:-https://rosa.radicle.network}\"\nSI_INSTALL_RAD=\"${SI_INSTALL_RAD:-0}\"\nSI_RAD_TIMEOUT=\"${SI_RAD_TIMEOUT:-5min}\"\n\n"
text sha2 "si_say() { printf '%s\\n' \"$*\"; }\nsi_die() { printf 'si: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\n\n"
text sha3 "if [ \"$(id -u)\" = \"0\" ]; then si_die \"refusing to run as root; run it as your own user\"; fi\ncase \"$SI_ONLY\" in all|core) ;; *) si_die \"SI_ONLY must be all or core\" ;; esac\ncommand -v git >/dev/null 2>&1 || si_die \"git is required: https://git-scm.com\"\nsi_rad=0\nif command -v rad >/dev/null 2>&1; then si_rad=1; fi\n\n"
text sha4 "si_say \"Sovereign Intelligence. GitHub censored me. I demand to be heard.\"\nsi_say \"\"\nsi_say \"This will:\"\nsi_say \"  1. make one directory, $SI_DIR, and put everything in it (no sudo, nothing else touched)\"\nif [ \"$SI_ONLY\" = \"core\" ]; then si_say \"  2. fetch the "
text shb0 " core projects\"; else si_say \"  2. fetch all "
text shc0 " public projects (SI_ONLY=core fetches only the "
text shd0 " core ones)\"; fi\nif [ \"$si_rad\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  si_say \"     peer-to-peer with rad clone, falling back to git clone from $SI_HTTP, then $SI_HTTP2\"\nelse\n  si_say \"     with git clone from $SI_HTTP, then $SI_HTTP2 (rad not found; with Radicle it fetches peer-to-peer)\"\nfi\nsi_say \"  3. check out the commit the manifest names for each project and print OK or MISMATCH\"\nsi_say \"\"\n\n"
text shd1 "mkdir -p -- \"$SI_DIR\"\ncd -- \"$SI_DIR\"\nsi_ok=0\nsi_bad=0\nsi_miss=0\n\n"
text shd2 "si_check() {\n  si_got=\"$(git -C \"$1\" rev-parse HEAD 2>/dev/null || true)\"\n  if [ \"$si_got\" = \"$2\" ]; then\n    si_say \"OK        $1 $2\"\n    si_ok=$((si_ok + 1))\n  else\n    si_say \"MISMATCH  $1 manifest $2, checkout ${si_got:-none}\"\n    si_bad=$((si_bad + 1))\n  fi\n}\n\nsi_fresh() {\n  si_tip=\"$(git -C \"$1\" rev-parse HEAD 2>/dev/null || true)\"\n  if [ \"$si_tip\" != \"$2\" ] && git -C \"$1\" checkout --quiet --detach \"$2\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    si_say \"$1: checked out the manifest commit; its branch has moved on to $si_tip\"\n  fi\n  si_check \"$1\" \"$2\"\n}\n\n"
text shd3 "si_repo() {\n  if [ \"$SI_ONLY\" = \"core\" ] && [ \"$4\" != \"core\" ]; then return 0; fi\n  if [ -e \"$1\" ]; then\n    si_say \"$1: already here, checking it\"\n    si_check \"$1\" \"$3\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n  if [ \"$si_rad\" = \"1\" ]; then\n    si_say \"$1: rad clone $2\"\n    if rad clone --timeout \"$SI_RAD_TIMEOUT\" \"$2\" \"$1\" </dev/null; then\n      si_fresh \"$1\" \"$3\"\n      return 0\n    fi\n    rm -rf -- \"./$1\"\n  fi\n  for si_src in \"$SI_HTTP\" \"$SI_HTTP2\"; do\n    si_say \"$1: git clone $si_src/${2#rad:}.git\"\n    if git clone --quiet -- \"$si_src/${2#rad:}.git\" \"$1\" </dev/null; then\n      si_fresh \"$1\" \"$3\"\n      return 0\n    fi\n    rm -rf -- \"./$1\"\n  done\n  si_say \"MISSING   $1 $2 (could not fetch it; this Radicle ID finds it on any seed)\"\n  si_miss=$((si_miss + 1))\n}\n\n"
text she0 "\n"
text she1 "si_say \"\"\nsi_say \"Done in $(pwd): $si_ok OK, $si_bad MISMATCH, $si_miss MISSING.\"\nif [ \"$si_miss\" -gt 0 ]; then\n  if [ \"$si_rad\" = \"1\" ]; then\n    si_say \"Is your Radicle node running? Start it with: rad node start\"\n    si_say \"Then run this again; projects already here are only checked.\"\n  else\n    si_say \"\"\n    si_say \"Radicle fetches the missing projects peer-to-peer: https://radicle.xyz\"\n    si_say \"Its official installer, run as your own user:\"\n    si_say \"  curl -sSf https://radicle.xyz/install | sh\"\n    if [ \"$SI_INSTALL_RAD\" = \"1\" ]; then\n      si_say \"SI_INSTALL_RAD=1: running it now.\"\n      curl -sSf https://radicle.xyz/install | sh\n      si_say \"Next: rad auth, then rad node start, then run this again.\"\n    else\n      si_say \"This script does not run it unless you set SI_INSTALL_RAD=1.\"\n    fi\n  fi\nfi\nif [ \"$si_bad\" -gt 0 ]; then exit 2; fi\nif [ \"$si_miss\" -gt 0 ]; then exit 3; fi\nexit 0\n"

note die: report m and up to 200 bytes of src from o on stderr, then exit 1
fn die m view uchar * o ulong n ulong to void
k = n
if gt k 200
k = 200
end
w = write 2 tsi 0 len tsi
w = write 2 m 0 len m
if gt k 0
w = write 2 src o k
end
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end

note dief: report m and the current path on stderr, then exit 1
fn dief m view uchar * to void
w = write 2 tsi 0 len tsi
w = write 2 m 0 len m
w = write 2 pb 0 get pbn 0
w = write 2 tnl 0 len tnl
exit 1
end

note setpath: copy command-line argument ai into pb
fn setpath ai ulong to void
n = argread ai pb 0 4096
if le n 0
die targ 0 0
end
put pbn 0 ulong n
end

note load: append the file named by argument ai to src and return where it starts
fn load ai ulong to ulong
setpath ai
fd = fopen pb 0 get pbn 0 0 0
if lt fd 0
dief topen
end
s = get srcn 0
p = s
while lt p 4194304 bound 4194305
k = read int fd src p sub 4194304 p
if lt k 0
dief tread
end
if eq k 0
break
end
p = add p ulong k
end
c = fclose int fd
if ge p 4194304
dief tbig
end
put srcn 0 p
ret s
end

note wout: write ob to the file named by argument ai (created or truncated, mode 0644), then empty ob
fn wout ai ulong to void
setpath ai
fd = fopen pb 0 get pbn 0 577 420
if lt fd 0
dief topen
end
n = get obn 0
p = ulong 0
while lt p n bound 4194305
k = write int fd ob p sub n p
if le k 0
dief twrite
end
p = add p ulong k
end
c = fclose int fd
if ne c 0
dief twrite
end
put obn 0 0
end

note em: append a text to ob
fn em t view uchar * to void
p = get obn 0
n = len t
if gt n sub 4194304 p
die toverf 0 0
end
for i ulong n
put ob add p i get t i
end
put obn 0 add p n
end

note ems: append n bytes of src from o to ob
fn ems o ulong n ulong to void
p = get obn 0
if gt n sub 4194304 p
die toverf 0 0
end
for i ulong n
put ob add p i get src add o i
end
put obn 0 add p n
end

note emb: append one byte to ob
fn emb c uchar to void
p = get obn 0
if ge p 4194304
die toverf 0 0
end
put ob p c
put obn 0 add p 1
end

note emu: append v in decimal to ob
fn emu v ulong to void
d = new uchar 20 0
x = v
put d 0 uchar add rem x 10 48
k = ulong 1
x = div x 10
while gt x 0 bound 20
put d k uchar add rem x 10 48
k = add k 1
x = div x 10
end
while gt k 0 bound 20
k = sub k 1
emb get d k
end
end

note eqt: do the n bytes of src at o equal the text t
fn eqt o ulong n ulong t view uchar * to bool
if ne n len t
ret false
end
for i ulong n
if ne get src add o i get t i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note eqs: are two slices of src equal
fn eqs a ulong an ulong b ulong bn ulong to bool
if ne an bn
ret false
end
for i ulong an
if ne get src add a i get src add b i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note find: first place in src from s, before e, where t starts; e when there is none
fn find s ulong e ulong t view uchar * to ulong
n = len t
if lt sub e s n
ret e
end
lp = sub e n
p = s
while le p lp bound 4194305
if eqt p n t
ret p
end
p = add p 1
end
ret e
end

note eol: the end of the line that starts at p (its newline, or e)
fn eol p ulong e ulong to ulong
q = p
while lt q e bound 4194305
if eq get src q 10
ret q
end
q = add q 1
end
ret e
end

fn isaln c uchar to bool
ret or or and ge c 48 le c 57 and ge c 65 le c 90 and ge c 97 le c 122
end

note okname: 1..64 bytes of letters, digits, dot, dash, underscore; not ".", "..", or a leading dash
fn okname o ulong n ulong to bool
if or eq n 0 gt n 64
ret false
end
if eq get src o 45
ret false
end
for i ulong n
c = get src add o i
if not or isaln c or eq c 46 or eq c 45 eq c 95
ret false
end
end
if eqt o n tdot
ret false
end
ret not eqt o n tdotdot
end

note okrid: "rad:z" then letters and digits, 6..64 bytes in all
fn okrid o ulong n ulong to bool
if or lt n 6 gt n 64
ret false
end
if not eqt o 5 tradz
ret false
end
for i ulong sub n 5
if not isaln get src add add o 5 i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note okhex: exactly 40 lowercase hex digits
fn okhex o ulong n ulong to bool
if ne n 40
ret false
end
for i ulong n
c = get src add o i
if not or and ge c 48 le c 57 and ge c 97 le c 102
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note okdesc: at most 512 bytes, none of them a control byte
fn okdesc o ulong n ulong to bool
if gt n 512
ret false
end
for i ulong n
c = get src add o i
if or lt c 32 eq c 127
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note fldo, fldn: offset and length of field k of record r
fn fldo r ulong k ulong to ulong
ret get rec add mul r 12 mul k 2
end

fn fldn r ulong k ulong to ulong
ret get rec add add mul r 12 mul k 2 1
end

fn kindof r ulong to ulong
ret get rec add mul r 12 10
end

note inventory_row: split one inventory line [p, q) into its five fields and check them
fn inventory_row p ulong q ulong to void
r = get nrec 0
if ge r 1024
die tmany p sub q p
end
b = mul r 12
k = ulong 0
st = p
i = p
while le i q bound 4194305
c = uchar 10
if lt i q
c = get src i
end
if or eq c 9 eq c 10
if ge k 5
die tcols p sub q p
end
put rec add b mul k 2 st
put rec add add b mul k 2 1 sub i st
k = add k 1
st = add i 1
end
i = add i 1
end
if ne k 5
die tcols p sub q p
end
if not okname get rec b get rec add b 1
die tbname p sub q p
end
if not okrid get rec add b 2 get rec add b 3
die tbrid p sub q p
end
if not or eqt get rec add b 4 get rec add b 5 tpublic eqt get rec add b 4 get rec add b 5 tprivat
die tbvis p sub q p
end
if not okhex get rec add b 6 get rec add b 7
die tbhead p sub q p
end
if not okdesc get rec add b 8 get rec add b 9
die tbdesc p sub q p
end
put rec add b 10 0
put rec add b 11 0
put nrec 0 add r 1
end

note parse_inventory: every line of [s, e) that is neither empty nor a # comment is a project
fn parse_inventory s ulong e ulong to void
p = s
while lt p e bound 4194305
q = eol p e
if lt p q
if ne get src p 35
inventory_row p q
end
end
p = add q 1
end
end

note order_row: one ORDER line [p, q), "core TAB name" or "deny TAB name"
fn order_row p ulong q ulong to void
t = find p q ttab
if eq t q
die tbord p sub q p
end
o = add t 1
n = sub q o
if not okname o n
die tbord p sub q p
end
if eqt p sub t p tcore
k = get ncor 0
if ge k 64
die tmore p sub q p
end
put cor mul k 2 o
put cor add mul k 2 1 n
put ncor 0 add k 1
ret
end
if eqt p sub t p tdeny
k = get nden 0
if ge k 64
die tmore p sub q p
end
put den mul k 2 o
put den add mul k 2 1 n
put nden 0 add k 1
ret
end
if eqt p sub t p tlead
if ne get nled 0 0
die tmore p sub q p
end
put led 0 o
put led 1 n
put nled 0 1
ret
end
die tbord p sub q p
end

fn parse_order s ulong e ulong to void
p = s
while lt p e bound 4194305
q = eol p e
if lt p q
if ne get src p 35
order_row p q
end
end
p = add q 1
end
end

note vet_row: one VETTED line [p, q); "| name | rid | branch | head |" with a good name,
note RID and 40-digit head is kept, any other line is ignored
fn vet_row p ulong q ulong to void
if lt sub q p 8
ret
end
if ne get src p 124
ret
end
a = add p 2
b = find a q tbar
if eq b q
ret
end
c = add b 3
d = find c q tbar
if eq d q
ret
end
f = find add d 3 q tbar
if eq f q
ret
end
g = add f 3
h = find g q tbare
if eq h q
ret
end
if not okname a sub b a
ret
end
if not okrid c sub d c
ret
end
if not okhex g sub h g
ret
end
k = get nvet 0
if ge k 1024
die tmvet p sub q p
end
put vet mul k 4 a
put vet add mul k 4 1 sub b a
put vet add mul k 4 2 c
put vet add mul k 4 3 sub d c
put nvet 0 add k 1
end

note parse_vetted: the vetted rows are those before the first "## " section line,
note so WITHDRAWN, Extra branches and any later section are never vetted
fn parse_vetted s ulong e ulong to void
p = s
while lt p e bound 4194305
q = eol p e
if ge sub q p 3
if eq find p add p 3 tsec p
ret
end
end
vet_row p q
p = add q 1
end
end

note vetted: are record r's name and RID both on one VETTED row
fn vetted r ulong to bool
nmo = fldo r 0
nmn = fldn r 0
ro = fldo r 1
rn = fldn r 1
nv = get nvet 0
for j ulong nv
vo = get vet mul j 4
vn = get vet add mul j 4 1
if eqs nmo nmn vo vn
vo = get vet add mul j 4 2
vn = get vet add mul j 4 3
if eqs ro rn vo vn
ret true
end
end
end
ret false
end

note check_unique: no two projects share a name or a RID
fn check_unique to void
nr = get nrec 0
for a ulong nr
for b ulong a
if samefld a b 0
die tdupn fldo a 0 fldn a 0
end
if samefld a b 1
die tdupr fldo a 1 fldn a 1
end
end
end
end

note samefld: do records a and b agree on field k
fn samefld a ulong b ulong k ulong to bool
ao = fldo a k
an = fldn a k
bo = fldo b k
bn = fldn b k
ret eqs ao an bo bn
end

note denied: is record r named by a deny line
fn denied r ulong to bool
o = fldo r 0
n = fldn r 0
nd = get nden 0
for j ulong nd
dno = get den mul j 2
dn = get den add mul j 2 1
if eqs o n dno dn
ret true
end
end
ret false
end

note mark_hidden: private, denied and unvetted projects get kind 2 and are never listed
fn mark_hidden to void
nr = get nrec 0
for r ulong nr
kd = ulong 0
if not eqt fldo r 2 fldn r 2 tpublic
kd = 2
end
if denied r
kd = 2
end
if not vetted r
kd = 2
end
put rec add mul r 12 10 kd
end
end

note order_core: each core name must be a listed public project; they lead, in ORDER's order
fn order_core to void
nr = get nrec 0
nc = get ncor 0
for j ulong nc
co = get cor mul j 2
cn = get cor add mul j 2 1
hit = nr
for r ulong nr
if eqs fldo r 0 fldn r 0 co cn
hit = r
end
end
if eq hit nr
die tcmiss co cn
end
if ne kindof hit 0
die tcpriv co cn
end
put rec add mul hit 12 10 1
put rec add mul hit 12 11 j
put seq j hit
end
put nseq 0 nc
end

note order_rest: the other public projects follow, in inventory order
fn order_rest to void
nr = get nrec 0
k = get nseq 0
for r ulong nr
if eq kindof r 0
put seq k r
k = add k 1
end
end
put nseq 0 k
end

note emit_desc: a description for a Markdown table cell, with | escaped
fn emit_desc r ulong to void
o = fldo r 4
n = fldn r 4
for i ulong n
c = get src add o i
if eq c 124
emb 92
end
emb c
end
end

note gen_index: the README project table
fn gen_index to void
n = get nseq 0
em ix1
emu n
em ix2
emu get ncor 0
em ix3
for i ulong n
r = get seq i
em ix4
emu add i 1
em ix5
ems fldo r 0 fldn r 0
em ix6
if eq kindof r 1
em ix7
end
em ix8
ems fldo r 1 fldn r 1
em ix9
ems fldo r 3 7
em ix10
emit_desc r
em ix11
end
end

note findlead: the listed public project named [o, o+n), or nrec when there is none
fn findlead o ulong n ulong to ulong
nr = get nrec 0
hit = nr
for r ulong nr
if lt kindof r 2
if eqs fldo r 0 fldn r 0 o n
hit = r
end
end
end
ret hit
end

note gen_lead: the clone line of the lead project, or a note that it is not on Radicle yet
fn gen_lead to void
if eq get nled 0 0
ret
end
lo = get led 0
ln = get led 1
r = findlead lo ln
if eq r get nrec 0
em ld0
ems lo ln
em ld1
ret
end
em ld2
ems fldo r 1 fldn r 1
em ld3
ems lo ln
em ld4
ems fldo r 1 fldn r 1
em ld5
ems fldo r 1 fldn r 1
em ld6
end

note gen_agent: the link to the lead project's AGENT-PROMPT.md, or a note that it is not on Radicle yet
fn gen_agent to void
if eq get nled 0 0
ret
end
lo = get led 0
ln = get led 1
r = findlead lo ln
if eq r get nrec 0
em ld0
ems lo ln
em ag3
ret
end
em ag1
ems fldo r 1 fldn r 1
em ag2
end

note mark: where t first starts in src [s, e); a README without it dies
fn mark s ulong e ulong t view uchar * to ulong
y = find s e t
if eq y e
die tnomark 0 0
end
ret y
end

note gen_readme: README [rs, re) with the lead block, the agent link and the index put between their markers
fn gen_readme rs ulong re ulong to void
be = add mark rs re tlbeg len tlbeg
x = mark be re tlend
be2 = add mark x re tabeg len tabeg
x2 = mark be2 re taend
be3 = add mark x2 re tbeg len tbeg
x3 = mark be3 re tend
ems rs sub be rs
emb 10
gen_lead
ems x sub be2 x
emb 10
gen_agent
ems x2 sub be3 x2
emb 10
gen_index
ems x3 sub re x3
end

note gen_repos: the manifest, name TAB rid TAB head TAB tier TAB description
fn gen_repos to void
em rphdr
n = get nseq 0
for i ulong n
r = get seq i
ems fldo r 0 fldn r 0
emb 9
ems fldo r 1 fldn r 1
emb 9
ems fldo r 3 fldn r 3
emb 9
if eq kindof r 1
em tcore
else
em trest
end
emb 9
ems fldo r 4 fldn r 4
emb 10
end
end

note gen_sh: the bootstrap script, one si_repo line per listed project
fn gen_sh to void
em sha0
em sha1
em sha2
em sha3
em sha4
emu get ncor 0
em shb0
emu get nseq 0
em shc0
emu get ncor 0
em shd0
em shd1
em shd2
em shd3
n = get nseq 0
for i ulong n
r = get seq i
em shr1
ems fldo r 0 fldn r 0
em shr2
ems fldo r 1 fldn r 1
em shr2
ems fldo r 3 fldn r 3
em shr2
if eq kindof r 1
em tcore
else
em trest
end
em shr3
end
em she0
em she1
end

fn main to int
if ne argcnt 7
w = write 2 tusage 0 len tusage
ret 2
end
ins = load 1
ine = get srcn 0
ors = load 2
ore = get srcn 0
vs = load 3
ve = get srcn 0
rs = load 4
re = get srcn 0
parse_inventory ins ine
parse_order ors ore
parse_vetted vs ve
check_unique
mark_hidden
order_core
order_rest
gen_readme rs re
wout 4
gen_repos
wout 5
gen_sh
wout 6
ret 0
end
